WEBVTT

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:30.500
I see no issue here.

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:37.620
You foolish child.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:38.720
Do as you wish.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:42.730
I humbly thank you for your mercy
in this matter.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:46.750
Apparently, you don't understand
a thing, Yasaburo.

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:50.270
I have always been kind to you.

00:00:55.340 --> 00:01:00.180
"Nasebanaru" to hito wa yuuga

00:00:55.340 --> 00:01:00.180
People say, "Where there's 
a will, there's a way"

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:03.570
Narugamama naseba ii

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:03.570
But things can just be how they'll be

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:16.280
Nagareru kawa ukabu kobune

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:16.280
A small boat floats along the river

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:20.180
Doko ni yukuno darouka

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:20.180
I wonder where it's going

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:25.410
Ikisaki nado yosou dekinu

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:25.410
I can't even guess its destination

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:29.650
Sorega omoshiroki koto

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:29.650
But that's why it's so fun

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:38.780
Kokorozashi wa takaku mokuhyou wa hikuku

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:38.780
My intentions are high, but my goals are low

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:43.830
Aho wo mazerya kekka

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:43.830
When foolishness gets mixed in

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:50.880
Yukai ni nareru

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:50.880
Everything will be merry

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:57.670
Narugamama ni sawagu mama ni

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:57.670
As things will be, as chaotic as they will be

00:01:57.670 --> 00:02:02.300
Toraburu suramo nenryou sa

00:01:57.670 --> 00:02:02.300
Even troubles become fuel

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:06.770
Namikaze tatanai jinsei wa

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:06.770
A life lived without any strife

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:11.270
Chotto bakkari tsumaranai

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:11.270
Can be a bit boring

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:16.020
Okiraku ni gokuraku ni

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:16.020
Carefree and blissfully

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:20.550
Kaze ni makasete ikou

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:20.550
Let's let the wind lead us

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:24.990
Kyou mo bakashite ikou

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:24.990
Let's go trick everyone again today

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:28.000
<b>Episode Ten
The Day the Trick Magister Is Chosen</b>

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:31.500
<i>Hello everyone, are you all doing well?</i>

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:34.000
<b>Kyoto-fu, Shimogamo Shrine
The Shimogamo family</b>

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:36.590
<i>I'm currently in Tomonoura in Hiroshima,</i>

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:39.870
<i>a port town which faces the Seto Inland Sea.</i>

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:43.520
<i>When I first left Kyoto,</i>

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:46.600
<i>it took everything I had
in order to stay transformed,</i>

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:49.600
<i>but now, I've gotten used to it.</i>

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:55.270
<i>The act of traveling to a different town
is great entertainment unto itself.</i>

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:56.960
<i>The other day,</i>

00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:01.990
<i>I met a tanuki who had come by boat
from Marugame in Shikoku.</i>

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:06.700
<i>I plan to ask if I can ride his boat</i>

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:09.660
<i>to Shikoku and visit the Kincho clan.</i>

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:12.290
<b>Kyoto-fu, Shimogamo Shrine
The Shimogamo family</b>

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:16.160
<i>Anyway, I am doing very well
and continuing my merry little adventure.</i>

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:20.240
<i>I hope you are all doing well, too.</i>

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:30.560
I would love for this little
gold general to sit right here.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:35.440
That will make things very interesting.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:38.360
Oh, is that so?

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:40.280
Then I'll just have to do this.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.790
Well, well...

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:46.700
Pardon me.

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:49.760
Oh, you're here, too?

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:51.820
That's quite the get-up.

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:54.150
Are you going mountain climbing?

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:58.820
If you aren't properly equipped to go
into the research forest, you'll get lost.

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:05.540
I often think that doing away with body hair
was a human evolutionary failure.

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:06.470
Oh?

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:09.810
Well, look at that modern marvel.

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:13.650
So warm...

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:16.530
Welcome.

00:04:16.890 --> 00:04:20.110
My, those are some splendid yuzu.

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:22.160
Well, it is the winter solstice.

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:25.320
Those who do not enjoy
yuzu baths are not human.

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:29.450
I don't like baths.

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:33.000
Bathing makes your head itch.

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:37.080
Wouldn't refusing to bathe
make your head itch even more?

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:41.320
Once you get past the initial itchiness,
it doesn't itch anymore.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:44.590
It's all about enduring that first step.

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:47.000
My, how filthy.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:49.550
I see. Is that how it is?

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:57.550
The year-end banquet
for the Friday Club is drawing near.

00:04:57.550 --> 00:05:00.440
I'm sure they're starting to get concerned.

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:04.530
I obviously have no intention
of capturing any tanuki.

00:05:04.730 --> 00:05:07.190
That was truly a splendid plan.

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:12.540
If you can keep evading them,
they'll be at a loss and soon lose heart.

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:13.980
Just deserts, right?

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:19.200
But since we're dealing with Jyurojin,
he might come up with a plan.

00:05:19.650 --> 00:05:22.050
Tenmaya-san is particularly suspicious.

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:23.770
Yeah...

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:25.550
If it comes down to it,

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:29.440
I plan to infiltrate the banquet
and save the tanuki myself.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:33.310
<b>December</b>

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:33.310
Tanuki love Christmas.

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:37.190
What they love most is that
they have no reason to celebrate.

00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:40.350
That is a wonderful thing.

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:42.940
Hello.

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:46.930
My name is Nanzenji Gyokuran.
Please excuse my sudden visit.

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:48.600
Welcome.

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:50.200
What the heck is this?!

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:52.580
I've never seen anything like this!

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:59.570
Who else knows I'm here?

00:05:59.570 --> 00:06:01.720
Just your family.

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:03.070
I see.

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:06.500
Running through the 36 views was not enough!

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:11.100
The name Yasaburo the Runaway was to
reverberate through the capital once more!

00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:16.600
I'm surprised you can run your mouth like
that after incurring Benten-sama's wrath.

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:19.000
That's my reason for living.

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:22.360
Yasaka-san was worried.

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:26.660
Sure, but he's also in a hurry
to push the duties of Trick Magister

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:29.360
onto Yaichiro and run off to Hawaii.

00:06:29.690 --> 00:06:31.530
Yes, well...

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:35.400
He didn't want to become the Trick Magister.

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:37.500
He's naturally eager to retire.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:41.000
Most tanuki wouldn't want
to be the Trick Magister.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:43.430
I mean, other than my weirdo of a brother.

00:06:43.430 --> 00:06:46.350
And because you did that
for your weirdo of a brother,

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:49.380
your life is hanging by a thread!

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:52.840
I'm pretty sure that you're
quite the weirdo yourself.

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:55.950
You really don't have room
to talk about Yaichiro-san.

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:59.390
Meaning the Shimogamo family
is a bunch of weirdos.

00:07:00.470 --> 00:07:04.000
So am I a weirdo for marrying
into that family of weirdos?

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:08.780
Akadama-sensei has excommunicated you.

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:11.840
I see.

00:07:12.430 --> 00:07:13.630
I'm not surprised.

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:19.410
Tengu have their pride,
and tanuki have their dignity.

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:22.700
Even though Sensei suggested
the impossible in the first place.

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:25.430
I'll wait until everything calms down.

00:07:25.430 --> 00:07:28.550
Sensei can't really live without me.

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:35.510
But this is the first time
that he's officially excommunicated me.

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:42.510
Gyokuran, will you bring Sensei
some things for me?

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:44.000
Of course.

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:46.590
Make sure he doesn't
run out of cotton swabs.

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:48.040
When he's out of them,

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:51.400
his ears get itchy, and he tends
to cause some whirlwinds.

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:54.450
Well, they're just gentle breeze, but...

00:07:55.020 --> 00:07:58.790
You must really love Sensei, Yasaburo-chan.

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:01.790
Don't tell anyone about that.

00:08:02.140 --> 00:08:03.560
I'll lose all respect.

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:08.000
<b>Kyoto-fu, Shimogamo Shrine
The Shimogamo family</b>

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:14.300
Gyokuran?

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:15.590
Forget something?

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:23.770
B-Benten-sama?!

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:52.010
<b>Kincho Shrine</b>

00:08:55.490 --> 00:08:58.010
Why are you crying?

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:03.100
Because it's a pity
that I'll have to eat you.

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:12.610
Oh, it was just a dream.

00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:17.720
<i>The day the Trick Magister is chosen.</i>

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:21.500
<i>In other words, the anniversary
of our father's death.</i>

00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:26.260
<i>In other words, the day of the
Friday Club's year-end banquet.</i>

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:32.550
The day has finally arrived.

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:37.360
I'll be off now.

00:09:37.770 --> 00:09:40.360
Don't perform any experiments
that are too rash.

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:43.020
You're going?

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:44.240
Yes.

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:46.530
After the advance celebration,

00:09:46.530 --> 00:09:49.650
I'll attend the elders' meeting
at the Nidaime's mansion.

00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:56.260
I've made reservations at Akegarasu.

00:10:00.170 --> 00:10:03.040
The day has finally come for you
to become the Trick Magister.

00:10:04.570 --> 00:10:05.950
I'll be off now.

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:17.070
I'm sure that you will end up
following in my footsteps someday.

00:10:17.880 --> 00:10:20.990
There are some foul tanuki
in the tanuki world,

00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:24.800
and you can be rather hard-headed yourself,

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:27.350
so I'm sure there will be a lot of fights.

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:30.600
But when you make an enemy

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:33.360
you must also make a friend.

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:38.720
When you make five enemies,
you must also make five friends.

00:10:39.220 --> 00:10:41.670
So as you keep making more enemies,

00:10:41.670 --> 00:10:45.120
and even if one day half
of the tanuki world is against you,

00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:47.070
look beside you.

00:10:47.070 --> 00:10:49.790
You have three younger brothers.

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:53.010
This is a very empowering thing.

00:10:53.830 --> 00:10:57.670
There will come a day
when that will be your trump card.

00:10:59.950 --> 00:11:02.760
I always feel a bit lonely

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:06.220
because I don't have that card for myself.

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:09.210
I couldn't trust my younger brother,

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:12.020
and my younger brother didn't trust me.

00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:15.030
When someone of your own blood
becomes your enemy,

00:11:15.030 --> 00:11:17.530
he will become the ultimate enemy.

00:11:17.980 --> 00:11:23.210
That's why you must always trust one another.

00:11:23.770 --> 00:11:25.600
Don't ever forget that.

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:27.290
Always get along with your brothers.

00:11:27.760 --> 00:11:32.290
After all, all of you have the same blood
running through your veins.

00:11:32.660 --> 00:11:36.220
Though, I guess it isn't blood that
you can be particularly proud of.

00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:50.850
Everyone's already here.

00:11:55.370 --> 00:11:56.040
Drink up.

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:57.610
Ah, there he is!

00:11:57.980 --> 00:11:59.790
You're drinking already?

00:12:01.310 --> 00:12:03.660
I guess the day's finally here, Yaichiro.

00:12:03.980 --> 00:12:06.120
Now all there is to do is wait.

00:12:06.380 --> 00:12:08.890
Congratulations on this event.

00:12:08.890 --> 00:12:12.120
It's a bit early for that, Kureichiro.

00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:16.450
There's no need to be overcautious
anymore, Yaichiro-san.

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:21.670
<b>The Trick Magister of the Next Generation 
is You, Shimogamo Yaichiro!!</b>

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:21.670
Let us drink to your
moderate success. Cheers!

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:23.680
Cheers!

00:12:30.910 --> 00:12:33.810
You're thinking about
your brothers, aren't you?

00:12:35.380 --> 00:12:36.960
How did you know?

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:38.610
Of course I knew.

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:41.900
Because you're always worried about them.

00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:45.800
Yasaburo-chan was enjoying
his life on the run.

00:12:46.230 --> 00:12:48.660
I'm sure Yajiro-kun is fine, too.

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:52.550
He's probably made it to Shikoku by now.

00:12:54.530 --> 00:12:55.760
Yeah...

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:12.470
<b>Highest Rank Kincho Shrine</b>

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:21.480
<b>Home of the 808 Tanuki</b>

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:30.990
This should be the place, but...

00:13:48.420 --> 00:13:50.740
Do you belong to the Kincho clan?

00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:52.890
I'm not anyone suspicious.

00:13:53.090 --> 00:13:54.020
I'm actually—

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:02.600
I thought you were a tanuki,
but you were a frog!

00:14:02.600 --> 00:14:05.150
I've never seen a frog that
could transform before!

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:08.660
You must be a famous frog
in the frog world, huh?

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:11.910
I'm a tanuki, not a frog.

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:16.960
I've never seen such a
slippery-looking tanuki before!

00:14:17.550 --> 00:14:20.460
I had transformed into a frog
for quite a long time,

00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:23.750
so whenever I lose my concentration,
I revert to being a frog.

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:26.700
I do actually have fur as a tanuki should.

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:28.760
Wow, you're weird.

00:14:29.030 --> 00:14:31.300
What a strange thing to happen.

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:33.990
Why did you stay a frog for such a long time?

00:14:33.990 --> 00:14:35.060
Because they're cute?

00:14:35.240 --> 00:14:38.040
I transform into a frog all the time, too.

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:40.220
Frogs are great.

00:14:40.220 --> 00:14:42.930
When they hibernate, they burrow into holes.

00:14:42.930 --> 00:14:45.820
They must be amazing creatures
that know all about holes.

00:14:46.420 --> 00:14:48.710
Though, eating bugs is really gross.

00:14:49.440 --> 00:14:51.530
I dug this hole myself.

00:14:51.830 --> 00:14:55.050
Father told me not to dig any holes,

00:14:55.050 --> 00:14:58.460
but I'd rather die than not dig any holes.

00:14:58.460 --> 00:15:02.250
I'm sure that I was born
into this world to dig holes.

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:04.820
It's so calming sitting
at the bottom of a hole.

00:15:04.820 --> 00:15:08.140
But I still haven't been able
to dig my ideal hole,

00:15:08.140 --> 00:15:12.020
so I've been ignoring my father
and digging diligently every day.

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:14.430
You must be an artist.

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:16.130
Yeah! An artist!

00:15:16.130 --> 00:15:18.520
There are so many things to say about holes!

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:22.940
And then there are some clumsy
people who fall into my holes.

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:28.690
I wonder why, but I feel
as though I can tell you anything.

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:36.300
You're one of the Shimogamo tanuki!

00:15:36.300 --> 00:15:38.940
You let me ride in the
Trick Eizan Train before!

00:15:38.940 --> 00:15:40.160
Don't you remember?

00:15:40.390 --> 00:15:41.040
Huh?

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:44.030
Aw, so you're one of the Shimogamo tanuki.

00:15:44.320 --> 00:15:47.040
Then I'll take you to Father.

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:49.780
Lalala, froggies!

00:16:16.030 --> 00:16:17.710
Oh, really?

00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:19.120
Heya.

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:20.100
Hello.

00:16:21.530 --> 00:16:27.050
All the rooms lined up here are
Shiramine Sagamibo-sama's inner parlor rooms.

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:31.170
The Kincho clan rents the rooms
from Sagamibo-sama.

00:16:32.370 --> 00:16:34.630
I wonder how large it is.

00:16:34.630 --> 00:16:39.890
It's so insanely wide that just
thinking about it makes me yawn.

00:16:39.890 --> 00:16:44.020
What's more, the size and
shape always change, too.

00:16:59.260 --> 00:17:00.830
He's Shimogamo Yajiro.

00:17:02.360 --> 00:17:03.390
'Kay, bye.

00:17:05.730 --> 00:17:07.350
It has been a long time.

00:17:07.670 --> 00:17:11.420
I am Shimogamo Souichiro's
second son, Shimogamo Yajiro.

00:17:11.420 --> 00:17:14.660
Well, well, if it isn't
one of the Shimogamo boys.

00:17:26.340 --> 00:17:27.770
The Trick Magister...

00:17:27.770 --> 00:17:30.800
My, Yaichiro sure has grown.

00:17:30.800 --> 00:17:34.320
If you have any problems, please let me know.

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:36.730
For a favor from one of Souchiro's sons,

00:17:36.730 --> 00:17:40.450
I will offer up as much fur as you need.

00:17:40.850 --> 00:17:44.710
I believe that Yaichiro will eventually
come to greet you himself,

00:17:44.710 --> 00:17:47.360
but he mentioned that he would like

00:17:47.360 --> 00:17:51.170
to maintain the relationship that has
continued through my father's generation.

00:17:52.970 --> 00:17:58.550
Souichiro-kun was truly
a magnificent tanuki.

00:17:58.550 --> 00:18:00.810
Indeed, indeed.

00:18:00.810 --> 00:18:04.390
But his younger brother, Soujiro...

00:18:04.390 --> 00:18:05.850
It's all very tragic.

00:18:06.550 --> 00:18:08.860
However, now my uncle has also passed away,

00:18:08.860 --> 00:18:12.110
and the Shimogawa and Ebisugawa clans
have made peace.

00:18:12.430 --> 00:18:17.200
So who's the head of the
Ebisugawa family now?

00:18:17.560 --> 00:18:22.370
Thankfully, the eldest son,
Ebisugawa Kureichiro, has returned to Kyoto.

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:27.460
Well, that's a funny story.

00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:30.330
Oh, so you're finally awake?

00:18:31.100 --> 00:18:33.480
Kureichiro returned to Kyoto, eh?

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:45.440
I wonder whether Yaichiro is at
the tanuki election venue now.

00:18:50.080 --> 00:18:52.200
Hot, hot!

00:18:52.740 --> 00:18:54.770
Warn me before you show yourself!

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:57.820
I'm allowed to go wherever I choose.

00:18:57.820 --> 00:19:00.360
Are you implying that I need your permission?

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:03.120
I'm on the run right now, so...

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:07.290
It's your fault for being a tanuki and
picking a fight with that half-ass tengu.

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:08.660
Hey, hold it.

00:19:08.660 --> 00:19:11.770
I did all that for tanuki society.

00:19:11.770 --> 00:19:14.480
You only did it because you found it fun.

00:19:14.480 --> 00:19:16.800
It's your own fault
if you end up in a hot pot.

00:19:18.780 --> 00:19:20.820
Hey, come here a sec.

00:19:20.820 --> 00:19:24.260
I can't let anyone see me
in this pathetic form.

00:19:25.760 --> 00:19:26.900
Yeah, yeah.

00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:29.470
You're such a small man.

00:19:32.320 --> 00:19:36.110
So what are you doing here?

00:19:36.380 --> 00:19:37.760
I ran away.

00:19:37.760 --> 00:19:38.430
Huh?

00:19:38.770 --> 00:19:39.860
Why'd you do that?

00:19:40.230 --> 00:19:43.990
Kureichiro-niisan's acting super weird.

00:19:44.460 --> 00:19:46.680
He's been trying way too hard lately.

00:19:46.980 --> 00:19:48.870
And he's being way too clever.

00:19:49.020 --> 00:19:52.240
My two idiot brothers completely adore him

00:19:52.240 --> 00:19:54.140
and don't complain at all.

00:19:54.140 --> 00:19:57.320
Kureichiro's working hard
because he's head of the family now.

00:19:57.320 --> 00:19:59.940
Kureichiro-niisan never works hard

00:19:59.940 --> 00:20:02.830
and was never clever at all.

00:20:02.830 --> 00:20:04.720
It's been ten years.

00:20:05.040 --> 00:20:06.890
I'm sure even Kureichiro would change.

00:20:07.250 --> 00:20:08.420
And...

00:20:08.940 --> 00:20:13.930
Yaichiro-san came by to talk
about reinstating our engagement,

00:20:14.880 --> 00:20:16.900
but Kureichiro-niisan was against it.

00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:18.940
Well, I'm against it, too!

00:20:20.700 --> 00:20:22.940
I don't really care how you feel about it,

00:20:22.940 --> 00:20:25.240
but I thought it was strange.

00:20:25.590 --> 00:20:26.500
I mean,

00:20:26.500 --> 00:20:29.830
wouldn't it be perfect to further the peace
with the Shimogamo family?

00:20:30.180 --> 00:20:32.660
Well, yeah.

00:20:32.980 --> 00:20:34.920
I didn't like what was going on,

00:20:35.080 --> 00:20:39.660
so I left a note saying that I was
eloping with you and ran off.

00:20:39.660 --> 00:20:42.740
I'm sure my brother will be so surprised.

00:20:44.140 --> 00:20:45.260
Seriously...

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:48.940
You know, things are just
going to get complicated again.

00:20:48.940 --> 00:20:51.990
Why are you being so timid suddenly?

00:20:51.990 --> 00:20:54.380
The guy that you said you were eloping with

00:20:54.380 --> 00:20:56.400
doesn't even want it, so what gives?

00:20:56.400 --> 00:20:57.580
Shut up!

00:21:01.040 --> 00:21:02.780
Something feels strange.

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:05.610
It's as if I can hear music.

00:21:10.420 --> 00:21:11.450
What's wrong?

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:12.910
Kaisei?

00:21:13.460 --> 00:21:14.420
Kaisei?!

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:26.060
Let's go for one more, shall we?

00:21:28.360 --> 00:21:31.170
<i>While I was living
my carefree life on the run,</i>

00:21:31.570 --> 00:21:35.260
<i>I was often reminded about my eldest brother.</i>

00:21:36.360 --> 00:21:41.990
<i>My eldest brother had greatly regretted
involving me in this tengu incident</i>

00:21:42.340 --> 00:21:44.780
<i>and was concerned about what might happen.</i>

00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:48.810
<i>I told him it would all work out.</i>

00:21:50.760 --> 00:21:53.160
But it appears that it didn't
all work out after all.

00:22:04.580 --> 00:22:09.270
Tsuki wo medetewa toki ni wa nusunde

00:22:04.580 --> 00:22:09.270
While gazing lovingly at the 
moon, at times, she steals it

00:22:09.270 --> 00:22:14.060
Kimagure na kanojo wa ah

00:22:09.270 --> 00:22:14.060
Whimsical as she may be, ah

00:22:14.060 --> 00:22:18.580
Kawabe de hitori hoho ni namida

00:22:14.060 --> 00:22:18.580
As she stands by the riverside 
alone, secretly her tears

00:22:18.580 --> 00:22:22.950
Utsukushiku tayutau

00:22:18.580 --> 00:22:22.950
Quiver beautifully upon her cheeks

00:22:22.950 --> 00:22:34.660
Boku no te tori nagara 
kokoro wa dokoka ni ukabu

00:22:22.950 --> 00:22:34.660
She takes my hand, as her 
heart floats away somewhere

00:22:34.660 --> 00:22:39.210
Kasaneta te ni wa mada nukumori

00:22:34.660 --> 00:22:39.210
I still feel that warmth from her held hand

00:22:39.210 --> 00:22:43.540
Setsunai yume no sono ato saki

00:22:39.210 --> 00:22:43.540
Somewhere beyond this sentimental dream

00:22:43.540 --> 00:22:53.220
Demo kimi no me wa harukana 
mirai wo miteitane

00:22:43.540 --> 00:22:53.220
But you were already looking 
far into the future

00:22:53.220 --> 00:22:57.850
Zutto zutto oikaketayo

00:22:53.220 --> 00:22:57.850
I always chased after you

00:22:57.850 --> 00:23:02.190
Even when you were hurt

00:22:57.850 --> 00:23:02.190
Kimi ga kizutsuku toki mo

00:23:02.190 --> 00:23:11.570
Sotto mabuta ni yakitsuita kimi no sugata ni

00:23:02.190 --> 00:23:11.570
The vision of you that's 
softly imprinted on my eyes

00:23:11.570 --> 00:23:16.530
Ima mata tooku e to ah

00:23:11.570 --> 00:23:16.530
Once again, you fly far away, ah

00:23:16.530 --> 00:23:28.870
Tondeiku kimi wa hora Kanata no hito

00:23:16.530 --> 00:23:28.870
You are a person far beyond

00:23:31.120 --> 00:23:33.720
Tanuki are indeed pleasant little creatures,

00:23:33.720 --> 00:23:35.530
but they are truly foolish.

00:23:36.080 --> 00:23:39.410
I'd really like my air rifle returned
as soon as possible.

00:23:37.560 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>Episode Eleven
The Blood of the Tengu, the Blood of the Fool</b>
